# router_surge.py - byte-for-byte tape replay of a fixed, non-reactive
# opponent schedule that beat us decisively on the ladder.
#
# SOURCE. Episodes 108241294 and 108305356 (both losses for us, seat 0) were
# played by two different opponent submission IDs, 56005477 and 55976878,
# whose 720-step action streams agree on every farmer/hand move and differ
# only in 8 of 720 steps (457, 481, 577, 625, 626, 674, 685, 686) - all
# late-game SELL quantities/products, i.e. stock-dependent sell amounts, not
# schedule changes. That is a fixed, day/hour-keyed, non-reactive tape, not
# a reactive strategy: it beat us with $/day 4,270-6,383 late-season against
# our 2,362-4,841 (opp_reward 89,349 and 117,351 vs our 54,185 and 88,563).
#
# This file embeds the tape from the stronger of the two runs (108305356,
# opp_reward 117,351) and replays it verbatim, step-indexed by
# day*24+hour, with no market/observation-driven logic at all - the
# opponent's own schedule is the entire strategy.
#
# CAVEATS.
#   - This is exactly the class of "fixed schedule" agent this repo's own
#     Yuan-lineage tapes are built from (see router_yuan_nf.py): it plays
#     the same farmer/hand moves and market orders every game, regardless
#     of the actual opponent, board state, or market price. It cannot see
#     or react to a farm hand starving, a crop weeding out because a tile
#     assumption from the source game did not hold this game, or a market
#     collapsing because the real opponent this game is not the one whose
#     reactions are baked into the tape.
#   - Hands are padded/truncated to the actually-observed hand count each
#     step (mirrors router_yuan_nf.py's guard) since HIRE outcomes could in
#     principle diverge from the source game by one hand.
#   - Not intended to be routed on unlocked_shops or anything else - this is
#     a pure single-tape replay for measurement, per the assignment.

